# 13. Contingency matrix

| Trigger | Immediate response | Owner | Authority |
|---|---|---|---|
| Critical niche feature misses delivery | Activate approved compatibility or partner option; revise affected account plans | Product | Product and executive steering committee |
| Critical security vulnerability | Isolate affected component, patch if possible, restrict access, accelerate retirement if necessary | Security | CISO and executive sponsor |
| Strategic customer rejects replacement | Convene save team, validate economics, offer assurance package or defined exception | Account executive | Business-unit executive and CFO |
| Migration data loss or integrity failure | Stop wave, invoke rollback, preserve evidence, notify affected customer, conduct root-cause review | Migration office | Program executive |
| Replacement-product major outage | Pause migration waves, prioritize service recovery, extend parallel run where safe | Platform | CTO |
| Critical legacy engineer leaves early | Activate documented runbooks, cross-trained backup, retained advisor, and external support if needed | Engineering | CTO |
| Competitor displacement campaign | Deploy coordinated executive, product, commercial, and reference response | Sales and marketing | CRO and business-unit executive |
| Legacy exception becomes unsafe | Terminate or narrow exception under contract, provide emergency export and continuity support | Security and legal | CISO, legal, and executive steering committee |

